2026-10-21T12:47Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
The author's question on 2026-10-21 was whether gaze effort is proportional to
the risk. The design was settled earlier and is shipped: ticket 0902 (2026-10-03)
made the path-risk band a second axis next to size; `skills/review-pr/SKILL.md`
step 3 reads `skills/review-pr/panel-width.json` (Correctness only for at most
30 lines in at most 2 files and no pipeline path) and § Proportional depth maps
risk to seats (trivial: Correctness; standard: + Consistency; scripts: + Doc
propagation; substantial: all five). This ticket is not a new design. It fixes
that the shipped rules are not applied.

Evidence (2026-10-21, from the posted results and seat reports):
- PR 1568: two files of prose, 126 lines, band `low` in the gaze result; six seats
  ran (adherence, correctness, consistency, scope, doc propagation, red team),
  over several heads. A docs-only diff above 30 lines falls out of the
  "Correctness only" width and lands in a judged "proportional panel".
- PR 1471: 47 lines, mechanical interpreter swap in tests; five gaze runs, two
  of them escalations for a degraded panel.
- PR 1557 (33 lines, a wording rule in `skills/`), PR 1553 (docs and a ticket): four
  and three runs. `panel-width.json` treats every `skills/**` path as a pipeline
  path, so a wording fix is priced like code that decides what merges.
- Gaze's own text (`references/setup-and-breaker.md`) says the band is carried to the
  gate and "never used to skip a phase"; the band no longer scales the battery.
  Whether the earlier ticket 0902 rule (a low band lowers one rung) was dropped in
  the gaze shrink or earlier is not established.
- Where the full panel was worth it: PR 1564 (merge gate) and PR 1566 (guard hook)
  found real fail-open defects.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Re-read ticket 0902 and the shipped width and depth rules, and record in the
      ticket log what is in force and what the gaze shrink dropped, if anything.
- [ ] The seat set is chosen by an objective rule from three inputs the skill can
      compute: the path-risk band, the size, and the kind of change (documentation
      or tests only; skill, rule or workflow wording; code or hooks that can fail
      open). Documentation-only and mechanical test-only diffs: at most
      Correctness and Consistency, whatever their size. Wording changes in skills
      and rules: Correctness and Consistency. Red team only on code that can fail
      open (merge, gate, hooks, deletion, credentials). The cross-family read stays
      for that last kind.
- [ ] `skills/review-pr/panel-width.json` stops treating every `skills/**` and
      `rules/**` path as a pipeline path; the kind of change decides.
- [ ] The posted result and the review comment name the inputs and the chosen set,
      so the trail shows why the effort was what it was.
- [ ] One test per kind (documentation, wording, code) pins the chosen seat set,
      and a negative control shows a gate or hook diff still gets the full panel.
- [ ] A count of gaze runs per PR over the next 20 PRs is recorded in the ticket,
      against the 2026-10-21 figure of about three runs per PR since PR 1550.
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime; the cross-family seat
      stays a role, not a model name.
